WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.176 --> 00:00:04.926
(coins clinking)

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.477
- [Mark] Hey, Jerry.
- How you doing?

00:00:07.477 --> 00:00:08.793
- [Mark] You remember me?

00:00:08.793 --> 00:00:11.140
- I can't see your face. Let me see.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.363
I can get closer.
- [Mark] Can you see me?

00:00:13.363 --> 00:00:15.100
- Not really. Can you see about this eye?

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:15.933
- [Mark] I know.

00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:16.920
No, I photographed you.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.020
- Oh, you photographed me now?

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.860
- [Mark] Remember I
photographed you a while back?

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:20.693
- Wait a minute.

00:00:20.693 --> 00:00:22.630
Is you the one with the electric car?

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:23.463
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:23.463 --> 00:00:24.650
- That took me to-

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.600
- [Mark] I took you to Culver City.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.091
- I got you. I got you.

00:00:28.091 --> 00:00:31.407
I really like, it was like that goon.

00:00:31.407 --> 00:00:32.810
I ain't seen you in a while. How you been?

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:33.850
- [Mark] I'm good. How you been, man?

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:34.776
- Okay now.

00:00:34.776 --> 00:00:37.390
You got your electric car
in Culver City. Studio!

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.396
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:38.396 --> 00:00:39.630
- And you just restless.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.550
- [Mark] That's right.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:41.518
- Nah, I got you.

00:00:41.518 --> 00:00:42.634
- [Mark] Yeah. I have
the prints on the wall.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:43.787
- [Jerry] How'd your photo come out?

00:00:43.787 --> 00:00:45.120
- [Mark] The photo turned out great.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.437
The next time I see you, I'll show you.

00:00:49.503 --> 00:00:52.615
(talking fades out)
- [Mark] Tell me your story.

00:00:52.615 --> 00:00:55.270
You and I, we've talked several times now,

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:56.970
but I don't really know exactly

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.900
the full details of what
happened to you five years ago.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.278
- Okay. I was sitting at a bus stop.

00:01:05.278 --> 00:01:06.780
Going home from work one night.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.830
- [Mark] Coming home from work.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:11.994
- A couple months later,
I woke up in the hospital.

00:01:11.994 --> 00:01:13.420
I thought I was dreaming.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.533
The doctor told me that I was shot

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:17.253
in the side of THE head with a shotgun.

00:01:17.253 --> 00:01:18.722
- [Jerry] You were shot
in the side of the head

00:01:18.722 --> 00:01:19.555
with a shotgun.

00:01:19.555 --> 00:01:21.447
- And he said the only reason I survived

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.713
because it was point blank range.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:27.760
He said, if was not point blank range,

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.310
my head woulda been out in the streets.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:32.500
- [Mark] And you'd be dead.
- I'd be dead, yeah.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.850
- I can't see that good
out of this left eye.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:38.040
My nose I cannot smell
or breathe out of at all.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:38.873
- [Mark] Right.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:43.210
- The skin here came off my leg.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.852
- [Mark] Is there a skin
graft from your leg?

00:01:44.852 --> 00:01:46.170
- My leg, and put it up here.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.120
Roughly right here.

00:01:48.184 --> 00:01:49.448
They screwed my head.

00:01:49.448 --> 00:01:51.948
I don't know if you can see the spot here.

00:01:51.948 --> 00:01:54.051
This about right here. Right here.

00:01:54.051 --> 00:01:55.166
It's about right here.

00:01:55.166 --> 00:01:56.762
Right here.

00:01:56.762 --> 00:01:58.913
The sewed my skull back together

00:01:58.913 --> 00:02:00.262
or something like that, man.

00:02:00.262 --> 00:02:02.324
- [Mark] Let me touch it.
- Sure, go ahead.

00:02:02.324 --> 00:02:04.011
- [Mark] It feels totally natural.

00:02:04.011 --> 00:02:05.049
- It's only right in here.

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:09.083
It did something, man,
to the spot right there.

00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:10.811
I wanna say they put screws
or something in there.

00:02:10.811 --> 00:02:11.644
I don't know.

00:02:11.644 --> 00:02:13.951
- [Mark] I wouldn't doubt
you got screws in there.

00:02:13.951 --> 00:02:16.774
There's got to be more than a few.

00:02:16.774 --> 00:02:18.446
- My front brain is gone.

00:02:18.446 --> 00:02:21.012
They took my front brains out.

00:02:21.012 --> 00:02:23.854
The doctor told me,
"Man, when you got to me,

00:02:23.854 --> 00:02:26.115
I could see your brains
was hanging out your head

00:02:26.115 --> 00:02:28.427
like they a snotty little kid."

00:02:28.427 --> 00:02:29.413
- [Mark] Your brain was what?

00:02:29.413 --> 00:02:30.513
- Hanging out my face.

00:02:30.513 --> 00:02:31.434
- [Mark] Hanging out of your face.

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:34.101
- My front brains, yeah. He told me, yeah.

00:02:34.101 --> 00:02:36.268
And they had to remove it.

00:02:39.194 --> 00:02:40.280
- [Mark] They removed it?

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:41.504
- Yeah. See my brain in the front.

00:02:41.504 --> 00:02:44.097
See the back brain is your main brain.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.920
That's your back brain.
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.970
- That's what you think with,
move with, do all this with.

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:52.180
If I lose my back brain,
if I woulda survived,

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:53.540
I might've been in a wheelchair.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:56.241
I figure, some guy in a
wheelchair use their tongue to-

00:02:56.241 --> 00:02:57.551
- [Mark] Yeah. But you can walk and talk.

00:02:57.551 --> 00:02:59.210
(talking fades out)

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.440
- [Mark] Before you'd
been shot, your life-

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.350
You were going to work, you know,

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.857
you had a nice apartment
somewhere, I assume.

00:03:05.857 --> 00:03:07.052
- I had a plain apartment like,

00:03:07.052 --> 00:03:09.200
a hotel apartment like, yeah.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.706
I had to be able to see this.

00:03:10.706 --> 00:03:12.740
I had to make airplane
parts at a machine shop.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:13.573
- [Mark] Airplane parts at a machine shop.

00:03:13.573 --> 00:03:15.533
- Yeah. Yeah. Called Duchess.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:18.143
And this happened.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:20.913
So I can tell you where I been,

00:03:20.913 --> 00:03:22.787
but I can't tell you where I'm going.

00:03:22.787 --> 00:03:23.810
You familiar with that, right?

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:25.037
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:26.158
- God is good though, man.

00:03:26.158 --> 00:03:27.220
Dangerous, man.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.350
- [Mark] So you're still in
a dangerous neighborhood.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:30.183
- Yeah yeah yeah yeah.

00:03:30.183 --> 00:03:31.240
- [Mark] On Skid Row. You're homeless.

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:32.090
- Yeah. Uh-huh.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:34.130
- [Mark] Where are you sleeping?

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.621
- I sometimes sleep at
the Federal Court Building

00:03:36.621 --> 00:03:37.617
on Hill and 1st Street.

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.839
- [Mark] Just like in the
corner of the building?

00:03:39.839 --> 00:03:41.919
- Yeah yeah, the corner of the-

00:03:41.919 --> 00:03:42.967
- [Mark] But basically on the street.

00:03:42.967 --> 00:03:44.651
- Basically the street, but see,

00:03:44.651 --> 00:03:47.032
you can't see it from the sidewalk.

00:03:47.032 --> 00:03:49.450
They have security at
nighttime, but that's okay.

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.210
But I gotta get out of there

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.589
at six o'clock in the morning though.

00:03:52.589 --> 00:03:53.673
- [Mark] So you got a good spot.

00:03:53.673 --> 00:03:56.337
- Yeah. I got a good
spot. Down here the way.

00:03:56.337 --> 00:04:00.780
- [Mark] So, I mean, are you frustrated

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.723
or bitter or angry about
what happened to you?

00:04:02.723 --> 00:04:04.803
- I can't help it. So I accept it.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:06.830
- [Mark] You were always this way

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.940
or you've come to accept that?

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:10.570
- I always been this way.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:11.820
- [Mark] When you woke up months later

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:13.860
and you realize you're missing

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.510
the right side of your face and brain.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.040
- And then I said, "Oh my goodness."

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.626
I'm gonna say something else.

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.926
I haven't looked at
myself in about two years.

00:04:23.888 --> 00:04:24.893
I haven't looked in a
mirror so I could see myself

00:04:24.893 --> 00:04:26.040
in over two years.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.260
- [Mark] Yeah. How's your vision?

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.320
Can you see?

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:31.000
- I can kinda see this right here.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.250
And I don't look at
myself in over two years.

00:04:35.121 --> 00:04:36.060
(indistinct)

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.250
I said, "Well, things happen."

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.637
I just gotta accept that, you know?

00:04:40.637 --> 00:04:41.873
And keep moving on.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.050
- [Mark] Your attitude is amazing.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.100
- Yeah. Have to, man.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.023
I can't change it.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.599
I can't stop living now.

00:04:49.599 --> 00:04:51.029
- [Mark] You know, whenever
I hear somebody complainin'

00:04:51.029 --> 00:04:54.248
about their tough life, I think about you.

00:04:54.248 --> 00:04:57.800
- Yeah, I can't stop
livin'. I gotta live long.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.410
Definitely.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:00.243
God is good.

00:05:00.243 --> 00:05:01.840
- [Mark] And help you out on the street?

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:02.673
- Sometimes, yeah.

00:05:02.673 --> 00:05:03.506
People like you come around

00:05:03.506 --> 00:05:04.685
and help me out a little bit yet. Yeah.

00:05:04.685 --> 00:05:06.500
- [Mark] I'm sure, you get
some people who are scared-

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:08.720
- [Jerry] Now some is and some ain't.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.900
Some kids like, they come and
talk to me and everything.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:15.857
And some will cry. (shouts)
But some will walk up to me.

00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:19.944
"Hi!" And talk to me. (laughs)

00:05:19.944 --> 00:05:20.777
"How you doin'?"

00:05:20.777 --> 00:05:21.610
"Okay."

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:22.443
"Bye!"

00:05:22.443 --> 00:05:23.276
"Bye."

00:05:23.276 --> 00:05:24.237
Some scared. Some not.

00:05:24.237 --> 00:05:25.070
(indistinct)

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:26.870
You know?

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:27.730
Vice versa.

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:29.532
- [Mark] So they never
caught the guy that shot you?

00:05:29.532 --> 00:05:30.365
- [Jerry] I don't think so. I don't know.

00:05:30.365 --> 00:05:32.604
I don't know who did it.
I don't know who it was.

00:05:32.604 --> 00:05:33.967
- [Mark] Did you see him coming?

00:05:33.967 --> 00:05:34.806
- [Jerry] No, no.

00:05:34.806 --> 00:05:37.772
The last thing I remember, I
was sitting at the bus stop.

00:05:37.772 --> 00:05:38.605
And wham!

00:05:38.605 --> 00:05:39.922
- [Mark] So you don't even
remember it happening?

00:05:39.922 --> 00:05:40.755
- I don't remember it happening.

00:05:40.755 --> 00:05:42.208
Next thing, I'm sitting at that bus stop.

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:44.474
That's all I know, I was at
the bus stop sittin' there.

00:05:44.474 --> 00:05:45.807
And that was it.

00:05:47.276 --> 00:05:48.283
And I was out of it, they said.

00:05:48.283 --> 00:05:51.040
They said I had a 23 hour surgery.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:52.500
- [Mark] 23 hour surgery.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.800
- 23 hour surgery. 23 hour surgery.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.640
- [Mark] They saved you.
- [Jerry] Yeah.

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:00.924
They said, "I saved you
in the hospital, man."

00:06:00.924 --> 00:06:02.814
They were the top hospital in the nation

00:06:02.814 --> 00:06:04.639
as far as head trauma.

00:06:04.639 --> 00:06:05.472
- [Mark] I'm sorry. Say it again?

00:06:05.472 --> 00:06:06.712
- [Jerry] They said, "Do
you know your hospital

00:06:06.712 --> 00:06:08.075
is USC medical center?"

00:06:08.075 --> 00:06:08.938
- [Mark] USC Medical Center.

00:06:08.938 --> 00:06:11.025
- [Jerry] They said they one
of the top three hospitals

00:06:11.025 --> 00:06:13.200
in the nation as far as head trauma.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.182
- [Mark] Oh, is that right?

00:06:14.182 --> 00:06:15.682
- [Jerry] What you said? Yeah.
- [Mark] For head traumas.

00:06:15.682 --> 00:06:18.583
- [Jerry] For head
traumas, basically yeah.

00:06:18.583 --> 00:06:20.560
- [Mark] You went to the right place.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.260
- [Jerry] One guy say he seen me.

00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:25.597
He said, "Man, I read about you."

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:30.263
He said, "They got you in the
medical miracle history book.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.390
For surviving what happened to you."

00:06:34.390 --> 00:06:36.193
He said me and this other lady.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.247
You ever hear about that
lady that the chimpanzee

00:06:38.247 --> 00:06:39.799
ripped her face off or
something like that?

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:40.703
- [Mark] Yeah, the monkey tore her-

00:06:40.703 --> 00:06:43.380
- He said me and her
is in a miracle medical

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:44.463
mystery history book.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.340
They make me survive what happened to us.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.583
- [Mark] Yeah.
- Yup.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:52.103
Amazing.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:56.084
- [Mark] So it kind of
derails your life a bit.

00:06:56.084 --> 00:06:58.817
- See, well I don't know.

00:06:58.817 --> 00:07:01.074
As soon as I get situated.

00:07:01.074 --> 00:07:04.074
I get together and I go on the road.

00:07:05.855 --> 00:07:07.209
Thing happen, you know?

00:07:07.209 --> 00:07:09.601
- [Mark] Things happen.
They happened to you.

00:07:09.601 --> 00:07:12.351
- And things happen unexpectedly.

00:07:14.637 --> 00:07:18.850
So, I may have taken this negative

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.443
and turn it into something positive.

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:26.000
- [Mark] What words of
advice would you give people?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.860
- Keep your trust in God.
That's the only advice I got.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.556
Keep your trust in God.

00:07:30.556 --> 00:07:32.410
Like the words say, "In God we trust."

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.320
Keep your trust in God.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.180
He's the way, the light, the truth,

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.150
and the only, only way.

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:37.983
That's it.

00:07:40.692 --> 00:07:42.017
- [Mark] If anybody could sell
me on that, man, you could.

00:07:43.298 --> 00:07:45.641
- Yeah, keep your light, man. Hey.

00:07:45.641 --> 00:07:48.214
They said, "There's
nothing new under the sun."

00:07:48.214 --> 00:07:50.166
Nothing new under the
sun. What's happening-

00:07:50.166 --> 00:07:50.999
- [Mark] I'm sorry. Say it again?

00:07:50.999 --> 00:07:52.478
- Nothing new under the sun.

00:07:52.478 --> 00:07:53.386
- [Mark] Nothing new under the sun.

00:07:53.386 --> 00:07:54.871
- That's in the Bible.

00:07:54.871 --> 00:07:58.897
See what's happening today happened BC.

00:07:58.897 --> 00:08:00.702
You know what BC means?
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:00.702 --> 00:08:03.047
Before the birth of Christ.

00:08:03.047 --> 00:08:04.894
This been happening all since back then.

00:08:04.894 --> 00:08:05.947
What's going on today,

00:08:05.947 --> 00:08:08.021
was happening way back in the days.

00:08:08.021 --> 00:08:09.548
Same thing.

00:08:09.548 --> 00:08:12.450
The Bible said there is
nothing new under the sun.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:13.283
They said-

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:20.260
It'll be weeks beyond years

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:22.970
will go by like months.

00:08:24.771 --> 00:08:27.340
Months will go by like weeks.

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.679
And weeks will go by like days.

00:08:29.679 --> 00:08:32.587
And you will not know
your summer or your winter

00:08:32.587 --> 00:08:34.122
or spring or fall time.

00:08:34.122 --> 00:08:36.106
You won't know which is which.

00:08:36.106 --> 00:08:37.833
That's all in the Bible, man.

00:08:37.833 --> 00:08:38.933
It's all in the Bible.

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:42.890
- [Mark] What would you look forward to

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:44.240
down the road for you?

00:08:45.748 --> 00:08:47.113
- Happiness. (laughs)

00:08:47.113 --> 00:08:48.067
Yeah. Happiness.

00:08:48.067 --> 00:08:48.900
- [Mark] I mean, do you wake up happy?

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:49.733
You seem to be.

00:08:49.733 --> 00:08:51.410
- Yeah. I have to. Have to.

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:53.090
Gotta keep it strong.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.260
- [Mark] I've seen it multiple times now.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.070
And every time I see you,
you seem in a great mood.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.640
- Yeah, I been in a great mood.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.671
I can't let this bring me down.

00:08:59.671 --> 00:09:01.087
- [Mark] Does ever get you down?

00:09:01.087 --> 00:09:02.717
Are there some days when you wake up

00:09:02.717 --> 00:09:03.833
and you're like, "Goddammit."

00:09:03.833 --> 00:09:06.920
- No, no, no, no, see. I have
all the excuse in the world.

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:10.315
- [Mark] I'm sorry. Say it again?

00:09:10.315 --> 00:09:12.020
- I have all the excuse
in the world to see it,

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:14.230
to be down, everything like that.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:15.465
You know what I'm saying? This here.

00:09:15.465 --> 00:09:17.013
But I don't.

00:09:17.013 --> 00:09:17.998
I don't use this as-

00:09:17.998 --> 00:09:19.750
You know what I'm saying?
I don't use that and this.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:20.840
No way.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:22.513
I'm just blessed to be alive, man.

00:09:22.513 --> 00:09:24.327
That's the thing. Advice
that made me so happy.

00:09:24.327 --> 00:09:25.690
- [Mark] Yeah.
- I can be dead, man.

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:26.647
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:09:26.647 --> 00:09:28.949
- I can be dead. (laughs)

00:09:28.949 --> 00:09:30.523
If I was dead, it's probably like I said.

00:09:30.523 --> 00:09:31.867
- [Mark] Or it could have been worse.

00:09:31.867 --> 00:09:33.093
- Alive, but in-

00:09:34.444 --> 00:09:35.947
You ever see a wheelchair use their tongue

00:09:35.947 --> 00:09:37.772
to get around and stuff like that?

00:09:37.772 --> 00:09:40.463
I could barely feed myself
or anything like that.

00:09:40.463 --> 00:09:42.740
A vegetable or something.

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:43.940
I haven't been that way.

00:09:44.797 --> 00:09:47.233
But God kept me. Spared my life.

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:50.719
Which is great.

00:09:50.719 --> 00:09:51.992
- [Mark] You're beautiful and amazing.

00:09:51.992 --> 00:09:52.930
- Yup. This is great, man.

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:54.080
You guys are good, man.

00:09:56.345 --> 00:09:57.695
You stay with me every day.

00:09:58.590 --> 00:09:59.817
What time is it?

00:09:59.817 --> 00:10:00.680
(Mark laughs)

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:02.247
- [Mark] Let's see.

00:10:02.247 --> 00:10:04.761
It is 12:47.

00:10:04.761 --> 00:10:06.370
- 12:47.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.203
- [Mark] I'll take care of you.

00:10:07.203 --> 00:10:09.541
You'll get a nice meal or two today.

00:10:09.541 --> 00:10:11.842
(talking fades)

